 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 335766,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>Birds and reptiles convert toxic ammonia to uric acid or a similar compounds. Insects, who live on land, also convert ammonia to uric acid. This is as opposed to fish, which excrete ammonia directly, without converting it to another substance.</p>\n<p>The conversion of ammonia to uric acid requires energy and is more complex than excreting ammonia directly.</p>\n<p>Based on this information, make a logical claim why these organisms could have evolved the conversion of ammonia to uric acid?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 848646,
     "content_html": "To have the ability to switch between uric acid and ammonia excretion."
    },
    {
     "id": 848649,
     "content_html": "To conserve water where water is in shorter supply."
    },
    {
     "id": 848647,
     "content_html": "To reduce the impact in their environment because ammonia is harmful than uric acid."
    },
    {
     "id": 848648,
     "content_html": "For living in symbiosis with plants, to which uric acid is important."
    }
   ],
